            "detectedLanguage": "en",
            "pageCount": 2,
            "processed": true,
            "summary": "This document is an Adverse Event Report Form detailing a serious reaction experienced by a 54-year-old female patient after taking the medication Neptazol. The patient has a history of hypertension and reported no known drug allergies. She was prescribed Neptazol at a dose of 20 mg once daily, starting from July 1, 2026, and stopped the medication on July 10, 2026. The patient developed severe facial swelling and a widespread rash on July 8, 2026, which is considered an adverse reaction. \n\nDue to the severity of the reaction, the patient required a visit to the emergency room and was kept under observation overnight in the hospital. Her vital signs indicate elevated heart rate and mild fever upon admission, but stabilized significantly within six hours post-treatment. The adverse reaction resolved after discontinuation of the drug and administration of antihistamines. \n\nThis document is highly relevant to a patient-safety review as it involves a serious adverse event that necessitated medical intervention. It raises concerns about the safety of Neptazol and its potential side effects, warranting further investigation. The information provided could inform regulatory actions and contribute to drug safety monitoring efforts."
        }
